<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>go-widgets – Wasm</title><link>https://go-widgets.github.io/docs/0.2/tags/wasm/</link><description>Recent content in Wasm on go-widgets</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://go-widgets.github.io/docs/0.2/tags/wasm/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>A browser tab</title><link>https://go-widgets.github.io/docs/0.2/surfaces/browser/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://go-widgets.github.io/docs/0.2/surfaces/browser/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;The toolkit is pure Go with no DOM dependency, so &lt;code&gt;GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm&lt;/code&gt; builds
it like any other target. Two ways to put the result in front of somebody:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="a-plain-canvas"&gt;A plain canvas&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="a-plain-canvas"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#a-plain-canvas" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/go-widgets/webcanvas" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;code&gt;go-widgets/webcanvas&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; blits an RGBA
framebuffer into a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;canvas&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and routes DOM pointer and keyboard events back
into the scene. No compositor, no &lt;code&gt;SharedArrayBuffer&lt;/code&gt;, no cross-origin
isolation headers: any static host serves it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-go" data-lang="go"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="cp"&gt;//go:build js &amp;amp;&amp;amp; wasm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;package&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;github.com/go-widgets/webcanvas&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;func&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;webcanvas&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;Run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;screen&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;myScene&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The scene implements &lt;code&gt;App&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;Size&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Draw(buf []byte)&lt;/code&gt;, and one method per
kind of event, each reporting whether anything changed so an unchanged frame
is not repainted. It may also implement &lt;code&gt;Ticker&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Animator&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Resizer&lt;/code&gt; or
&lt;code&gt;Scroller&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://go-widgets.github.io/gallery/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;gallery&lt;/a&gt; and
&lt;a href="https://go-widgets.github.io/docs/0.2/getting-started/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;app-template&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; run this way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="a-window-on-the-wasmdesk-desktop"&gt;A window on the wasmdesk desktop&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="a-window-on-the-wasmdesk-desktop"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#a-window-on-the-wasmdesk-desktop" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;On &lt;code&gt;js/wasm&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;a href="https://go-widgets.github.io/docs/0.2/surfaces/native-window/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;window.Open&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
returns a client of the &lt;a href="https://github.com/wasmdesk/wasmbox" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;wasmdesk/wasmbox&lt;/a&gt;
browser compositor. It allocates its surface in a &lt;code&gt;SharedArrayBuffer&lt;/code&gt;, says
&lt;code&gt;hello&lt;/code&gt; over its &lt;code&gt;MessagePort&lt;/code&gt;, waits for &lt;code&gt;welcome&lt;/code&gt;, paints into the shared
buffer and posts &lt;code&gt;commit&lt;/code&gt; — the whole surface, or only the damaged rectangles.
The compositor&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;input&lt;/code&gt; messages become &lt;code&gt;toolkit.Event&lt;/code&gt;, as on X11.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So an application written against &lt;code&gt;window&lt;/code&gt; runs unchanged as a native window
and as a window of a desktop in a browser tab. The
&lt;a href="https://github.com/go-widgets/desktop" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;desktop shell demo&lt;/a&gt; does exactly
that, from one source.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The protocol codec is covered at 100% on every platform. The live proof runs
headless Chromium against the real wasmdesk compositor: it spawns the client,
reads the compositor&amp;rsquo;s own composited pixels, clicks, and checks that the
click reached the widget.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>